==English==

===Noun===
'''stepdame'''
# A [[stepmother]].

[[vi:stepdame]]

Found in the opening lines of Shakespeare's Midsummer Night's Dream:
"O methinks how slow this old moon wanes! 
She lingers my desires (= she delays the fulfillment of my desires)
Like to a [[step-dame]], or a dowager (= a widow with a right to her husband's property or title),
long withering out a young man's revenue (living long enough to use up ...)"